    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1321">

                <pb facs="0893" n="777" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg777"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.6363/104.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Miller to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Tampico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-06-12T20:00:00-06:41">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 12, 1914, 8 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s June 10, 5 p.m. Meeting of oil associations last Saturday took no
                    action on $200,000 loan, but will hold another meeting June 13.</p>
                <p>All petroleum production involved is now in territory controlled by
                    Constitutionalists, but it is said that General Candido Aguilar is demanding
                    payments of tax known as “Vera Cruz State tax”.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Miller</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
